# camera

Portable synchronous grayscale camera interface. Pixels are row-major, one
unsigned byte per pixel, zero black and 255 white, with no row padding.
The caller owns the capture buffer; capture requires exactly width*height
bytes and a positive timeout in milliseconds. A failed capture leaves the
buffer contents unspecified. Providers return NotInitialized before initialize
and after sleep; sleep releases capture resources and can be called repeatedly.
Unbound lanes return Unsupported. Applications call selected_camera().
